course: dictionary
lesson: 12277
title: Formal words: contravene
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Contravene is a formal word, and you will meet it on signs, in news stories and in school rules. It means to break a law, a rule or an agreement. «Anyone contravening these rules will be asked to leave.» The word rules tells you what is being broken, and being asked to leave tells you it is serious.
explain: You can often swap contravene for a simpler word such as break. Try it: «Anyone breaking these rules will be asked to leave.» The sentence still makes sense, so you have found the meaning. Look for clues like law, rules or agreement near the word.
explain: Contravene is a verb, so it changes: contravenes, contravened, contravening. The noun form is contravention, as in «in contravention of the law», which means against the law. Write it correctly in formal writing.
fact: Contravene means to break a law, rule or agreement.
fact: Contravene is a formal word, so you will mostly see it in official notices, news and school policies.
fact: A rare second meaning is to go against an idea or statement.
fact: The verb forms are contravenes, contravened and contravening.
fact: «In contravention of» means against a law or rule, for example «in contravention of the safety rules».
exercise: «The sign says anyone who contravenes the rules will be asked to leave.» What does contravenes mean here? | Reads the rules aloud | *Breaks the rules | Helps to write the rules | Paints the rules on a wall
exercise: «The driver contravened the law by going through a red light.» Which word is the best swap for contravened? | cooked | hugged | painted | *broke
exercise: «Her idea contravened what the whole team had decided.» Which sentence shows the second meaning of contravene? | The team all agreed with her idea. | *Her idea went against what the team had decided. | Her idea was painted blue. | Her idea was lost in the post.
test: Which phrase uses the noun form of contravene? | *in contravention of the rules | against the wall | in the middle of the rules | under the table
test: «The company contravened the agreement it had signed.» What did the company do? | Signed a brand new agreement | Kept its promise carefully | *Broke the agreement | Made lunch for the team
exam: «Anyone contravening the safety rules on the trip may be sent home.» What does contravening mean? | Forgetting | Printing | Reading | *Breaking
